---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'TODO_DATE — set this to the date you actually publish these terms.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms &amp; Conditions" description="Terms and conditions for OMG GameHub, its tournaments, and mobile recharge prizes.">
  <section class="relative py-32 sm:py-40">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <p data-reveal class="font-display text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Legal</p>
      <h1 data-reveal class="font-display mt-4 text-4xl font-bold leading-[0.95] sm:text-6xl">
        Terms &amp; Conditions
      </h1>
      <p data-reveal class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-faint">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div
        data-reveal
        class="mt-8 rounded-sm border border-dashed border-accent/60 bg-bg-raised p-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim"
      >
        <strong class="text-accent">TODO_LEGAL_REVIEW</strong> — this is a working draft, not
        reviewed by a lawyer. Before this page goes live, have it checked against current Indian
        law for skill-gaming/contest terms, state-wise restrictions, and tax treatment of prizes
        (rules here change and vary by state). Everything below assumes tournament entry is{' '}
        <strong class="text-ink">free</strong> — no payment, purchase, or stake is required to
        play or to win.
      </div>

      <div class="prose-invert mt-12 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-dim [&_h2]:font-display [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:text-2xl [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h3]:font-display [&_h3]:mt-6 [&_h3]:text-lg [&_h3]:font-bold [&_h3]:text-ink [&_li]:mt-1 [&_ul]:mt-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_p]:mt-4">
        <p>
          These Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms") govern use of the OMG GameHub mobile
          application ("GameHub", "the App"), published by White House Gaming
          ("we", "us", "our"), including the in-app tournament and leaderboard system that
          awards mobile recharge prizes. By downloading, installing, or using the App, or by
          entering a tournament, you agree to these Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Eligibility</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of majority in your jurisdiction, to enter a tournament or receive a prize.</li>
          <li>You must be a resident of India with a valid, active Indian mobile number capable of receiving recharge.</li>
          <li>Employees, contractors, and immediate family members of White House Gaming are not eligible to win tournament prizes.</li>
          <li>We may restrict tournament participation in any state or region where such contests are limited or prohibited by local law.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Free Entry — No Purchase Necessary</h2>
        <p>
          Playing GameHub's games and competing on tournament leaderboards is free. No payment,
          purchase, in-app currency, or deposit of any kind is required to enter a tournament or
          to be eligible for a prize. Making an in-app purchase (if any exist elsewhere in the
          App) does not improve your chances of winning and is never required to compete.
        </p>

        <h2>3. How Tournaments Work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Tournaments rank players by in-game score or performance over a stated period, shown on an in-app leaderboard.</li>
          <li>Winners are determined solely by ranking at the close of the tournament period, as recorded by our systems.</li>
          <li>We may run multiple tournaments across different games, with different schedules, rules, and prize amounts, communicated in-app at the time.</li>
          <li>Our decision on scoring, rankings, and winners is final.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Prizes</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Prizes consist of mobile recharge (talktime/data) credited to the mobile number registered on your winning account.</li>
          <li>Prize values, denominations, and the number of winners per tournament will be stated in-app before or during the tournament.</li>
          <li>Prizes are not transferable, not exchangeable for cash, and cannot be substituted except at our discretion.</li>
          <li>Recharge fulfilment depends on your mobile operator and may take a reasonable time to process after a tournament closes.</li>
          <li>Winners are solely responsible for any tax liability arising from prizes received. We may deduct tax at source and/or report winnings where required by applicable law.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Fair Play</h2>
        <p>The following will disqualify an entry and may result in forfeiture of a prize already credited:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use of bots, scripts, emulator exploits, modified clients, or other automation.</li>
          <li>Exploiting bugs or glitches to inflate score.</li>
          <li>Operating multiple accounts to gain extra tournament entries.</li>
          <li>Any other conduct we reasonably determine to be cheating or fraud.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Changes &amp; Termination</h2>
        <p>
          We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any tournament, prize structure, or these Terms
          at any time, with notice provided in-app where reasonably possible. Continued use of
          the App after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          The App and tournaments are provided "as is." To the maximum extent permitted by law,
          White House Gaming is not liable for delays or failures in prize fulfilment caused by
          third parties (including mobile network operators), technical issues, or events
          outside our reasonable control.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of India. Any disputes are subject to the
          exclusive jurisdiction of the courts at Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about tournaments, prizes, or these Terms can be sent to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="text-accent underline">{site.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
